Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["defensive suppression", "suppression-conditional recommended mix", "counter strategy (best/avoid play types)", "adherence to recommended mix", "series-level win prediction"],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Does adherence to a suppression-conditional recommended mix predict series winning, with adherence measured without look-ahead?",
  "Is 54 series enough power to detect a plausible adherence effect on a binary series outcome?",
  "How should play-type labels derived from play-by-play points be built so they do not encode the outcome?",
  "Can the engine's recommendation be reproduced reliably enough (fidelity) to define adherence?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-003",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Record reports SQ2 decision-quality hit rate (engine top pt_shift vs team modal PT). Full-calibrated headline 69.8% (37/53); clean comparisons 64.1% (25/39); high-confidence 64.3% (27/42); uncalibrated archival 51.7% (31/60). Recorded failure mechanism C_artifact, risks LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD and SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER; no bootstrap CI computed. Verdict recorded as artifact_found."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Ranked playsheet validation over 10 series. Spearman rho=-0.0639, p=0.099717, n=665 (no clear full-rank signal). Kruskal-Wallis p=2.7e-05. Mann-Whitney BEST 1.257 (n=56) vs AVOID 1.092 (n=160), p=0.004018. Recorded limits: leakage, low measurement reliability, small sample; risks DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY, LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD, MEASURE_RELIABILITY, SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER. Mechanism unclear."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF37",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Possession-level test of a proxy engine on all regular-season games: gamma +0.0714 (SE 0.0057, p≈0) on 16,921 cells, with DiD +0.062 PPP. Recorded as inconclusive because proxy agrees with production engine on only 13/79 = 16.5% of cases, there is in-sample contamination of regular-season aggregates, and SEs are iid. Coverage: 30.4% no_rec, 33.8% ambiguous, 35.7% clear."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg (n=120 team-seasons). Headline dR2=+0.139 is recorded as leakage tracking DRtg (corr(leakage, DRtg)=+0.894); offensive-control components add only +0.005. Not a series-level or defensive-mix test; cited only as a leakage warning."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-003",
   "what_failed": "Scoring engine top pt_shift against the team's modal play type as a decision-quality hit rate",
   "why": "Recorded as artifact: apparent effect attributed to construction, selection or labelling flaw (C_artifact); leakage risk and small sample (n=53) with no CI. Uncalibrated and calibrated versions differ widely (51.7% vs 69.8%)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018",
   "what_failed": "Ranked playsheet counter ranking predicting which alternative scored better after a play type was suppressed",
   "why": "Full-rank Spearman null (p=0.0997); only a pairwise BEST>AVOID signal; mechanism unclear (E_unclear); leakage, low measurement reliability and small sample recorded as limits."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF37",
   "what_failed": "Matchup-conditioned PT picker tested on all regular-season possessions",
   "why": "Inconclusive: proxy fidelity to production engine only 16.5% (<70%); in-sample contamination; iid standard errors likely overstate precision."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068",
   "what_failed": "Team-level PCI explaining net rating beyond ORtg",
   "why": "Artifact: headline gain tracks defensive rating via leakage (corr +0.894); the baseline omitted defense by construction."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "No retrieved record tests whether adherence to a suppression-conditional recommended mix predicts series winning. The question is not already answered.",
  "Earlier engine-based evaluations in this project have repeatedly been flagged as artifacts or inconclusive, mainly for leakage, label construction, and small samples.",
  "The production engine's recommendations were not reproduced reliably by a proxy (fidelity 16.5%), so adherence as a construct has unverified measurement properties.",
  "Prior records show that recommendation coverage is incomplete (about 30% no_rec and about 34% ambiguous in SF37), which limits how adherence can be defined for every series."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Whether the effect exists, its size, or its sign for series-level outcomes.",
  "Whether adherence is measured without look-ahead in the current pipeline.",
  "Whether any record used series win/loss as the outcome. The retrieved records mostly use possession-level PPP, hit rates or team-season metrics.",
  "Any effect estimate for the 2025-26 playoffs, which were partial as of the question date."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "With about 54 series (binary outcome, roughly balanced adherence groups), the detectable effect is large, on the order of 0.35–0.40 in win probability (own rough calculation at 80% power, alpha 0.05). Plausible adherence effects are likely smaller, so a null would be uninformative.",
  "Multiple games per series and two teams per series make the 54 units non-independent. Effective sample size is smaller than the nominal count.",
  "Series winners are strongly tied to team strength, seed and health. Without controls, adherence could simply proxy for better teams (CONFOUNDING)."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The exact series count after exclusions (the nominal 2022-23 to 2025-26 playoffs would be about 60 series, so 54 implies exclusions that are not documented here).",
  "Full text of SF-APPS-003 and SF-APPS-018 was truncated in retrieval ('read_family for the full text'). I did not retrieve the full records, so details of their calibration and leakage handling are unverified.",
  "Whether the production engine's adherence labels for 2022-26 are time-stamped and free of hindsight. Not documented in the returned records.",
  "Whether 2025-26 playoff data needed for the study will be complete by the analysis date (complete from 2026-06-21)."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "Retrieved history showed that earlier engine-recommendation tests were flagged as artifacts or inconclusive (SF-APPS-003, SF-APPS-018, SF37), that proxy fidelity was low (16.5%), and that leakage was a recurring problem. Together with a power check for 54 series, this moved the decision from a straight test to do_not_proceed as posed. A narrower, pre-registered test with leak-free adherence and fidelity validation is the minimum viable step."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.15,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "54 series gives power only for very large effects (about 0.35–0.40 in win probability, own calculation). Games within series are correlated, so the effective n is lower."},
